  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 3, 'Delivering an integrated ecosystem of information systems and digital health solutions supports the PHC approach'. Four nested layers surround a figure labelled 'Centered around the needs of the care seeker'. From innermost to outermost: COMMUNITY LINKAGES AND ENGAGEMENT (community health workers, care seekers) holds patient portal, targeted messaging, CHW job aid, self-monitoring devices and capacity building; ORGANIZATION AND MANAGEMENT (primary care providers) holds clinical job aids, AI risk assessment, referral and coordination, and an electronic health record; SELECTION, DESIGN AND PLANNING OF SERVICES (health system decision makers) holds a dashboard and management information systems; DEFINING A TARGET POPULATION AND UNDERSTANDING THEIR NEEDS (policy makers) holds civil registration and vital statistics, and disease surveillance. Each solution carries a one-line purpose. A note says solutions can span more than one layer and are allocated to one only for illustration.",
